# NekoChat Reloaded — PC client

NekoChat Reloaded is an unofficial desktop client for NekoChat. It is made for people who want a Windows XP-style chat application instead of a browser tab.

It includes:

- rooms and direct messages;
- detached chat windows and voice calls;
- Windows XP-inspired themes, frames, icons, wallpapers, and interface assets;
- XP-style notification, login, call, and system sounds.

Visual assets are in [`assets/images`](assets/images); themes are in [`themes`](themes) and [`prebuilt`](prebuilt). You can add project screenshots to a `screenshots/` directory.

> This is a custom client, not the official NekoChat application.

## Build and run on PC

Install Node.js 20+ and npm, then run these commands from the repository root:

```bash
npm init -y
npm pkg set main=main.js
npm install --save-dev electron electron-builder
npx electron .
```

To create a Linux desktop build after checking that the client starts:

```bash
npx electron-builder --linux AppImage deb
```

The generated files will be placed in the `dist/` directory.
